  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Quad Critical and Emerging Technology Forum 01-24</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program focuses on the Quadrilateral Security Dialogue (or Quad) between the U.S., India, Japan, and Australia. While the Quad is imagined as a geopolitical mechanism by which to sustain established rules/norms in the Indo Pacific and as a means to counter China&apos;s adventurous foreign policy, thus far it has not achieved much beyond sending certain political signals and engaging in joint military exercises. This program seeks to discuss how the Quad can assist security cooperation efforts, Indo-Pacific economic efforts, and environment concerns in littoral/maritime areas. The program includes invitations to India, Japan, Australia, as well as additional invitees from civil society organizations and academic institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
